examples.question_text:
A circle has circumference $17$ cm. Find its diameter, correct to $3$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.8);
\draw (-1.8,0)--(1.8,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0.9,0) node[above] {$d$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circle has circumference $21.4$ cm. Find its radius, correct to $3$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.8);
\draw (0,0)--(1.8,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0.9,0) node[above] {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An arc has length $12$ cm and subtends an angle of $60^{\circ}$ at the centre. Find the radius, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(2.6,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(60:2.6);
\draw[thick] (2.6,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=60,radius=2.6];
\draw (0.55,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=60,radius=0.55];
\path (30:0.95) node {$60^{\circ}$};
\path (30:3.05) node {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.3,0) node[below] {$r$};
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circular wire has radius $10$ cm. A section subtending $216^{\circ}$ at its centre is cut out and bent into a smaller circle without stretching.
Find the smaller circle's radius, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(1.8,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(216:1.8);
\draw[thick] (1.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=216,radius=1.8];
\draw (0.45,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=216,radius=0.45];
\path (108:0.85) node {$216^{\circ}$};
\path (0.9,0) node[below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[->] (2.2,0.3)--(3.2,0.3);
\draw (4.4,0.3) circle (0.95);
\draw (4.4,0.3)--(5.35,0.3);
\fill (4.4,0.3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (4.85,0.3) node[above] {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A belt fits tightly around a circular tank of diameter $8$ m. It is lengthened by $3$ m and held in a circle with the same centre as the tank.
Find the gap between the tank and the belt, correct to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont]
\draw (0,0) circle (1.5);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) circle (1.9);
\draw (-1.5,0)--(1.5,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0) node[above] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (30:1.5)--(30:1.9);
\path (30:1.7) node[above right] {gap};
\path (0,2.15) node {loose belt};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
